{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01X35t86NXgGBdSr8veysvN9","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have successfully read all three files. Here's the complete content:\n\n## 1. **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml** (Requirements Specification)\n\nThis file defines the complete requirements for the `ts` (timestamp) utility. Here are the specific requirements you asked about:\n\n**R6.1 & R6.2 (Relative-time parsing and age output):**\n- **R6.1**: `-r` must scan each input line for known timestamp patterns and replace each match with a human-readable relative age string (e.g., \"15m5s ago\").\n- **R6.2**: Must recognize the following timestamp patterns from the Perl source regex:\n  - Syslog format: \"Jan  5 14:30:00\"\n  - ISO-8601: \"2024-01-05T14:30:00.000Z\"\n  - RFC 2822 with optional day: \"16 Jun 94 07:29:35 GMT\"\n  - Lastlog format: \"Mon Jan  5 14:30\"\n\n**R7.1 & R7.2 (Exit codes and error handling):**\n- **R7.1**: Must exit 0 on clean EOF from stdin.\n- **R7.2**: Must exit non-zero and print a usage message to stderr when an unrecognized flag is given.\n\n## 2. **cmd/ts/main.go** (Existing Implementation)\n\nThe current implementation includes:\n- Default timestamp formatting with the format `\"%b %d %H:%M:%S\"`\n- Support for `-i` (incremental mode), `-s` (since-start mode), and `-m` (monotonic clock mode)\n- Custom format string support with strftime conversion\n- Subsecond extensions handling (%.S, %.s, %.T)\n- Proper padding and text/composite spec handling\n- SIGPIPE handler installation\n- Support for the TZ environment variable\n\n**Currently NOT implemented:** \n- The `-r` (relative-time parsing) feature (R6.1, R6.2)\n- Requirements R10 (relative-time format override)\n\n## 3. **cmd/ts/ts_test.go** (Existing Tests)\n\nThe test file includes:\n- Differential tests against the reference `ts` binary (using `testutils.BuildBinary`)\n- Tests for default multiline, single line, partial last line, and empty stdin\n- Tests for custom format strings with subsecond extensions\n- Tests for incremental and since-start modes\n- Tests for monotonic clock mode combinations\n- A `TestMutualExclusive` test that verifies `-i` and `-s` cannot both be given\n- A `TestSIGPIPE` test that validates SIGPIPE handling\n- Custom normalizers for subsecond precision and elapsed time\n\nThe tests use `testutils.TimestampNormalizer` to handle dynamic timestamps in differential testing."}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8b561b2f-f834-4d72-8216-db7f5b3730de","uuid":"0ed54c2f-80c6-458c-9ca1-f8596cd6165a","timestamp":"2026-05-29T16:25:56.447Z","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to read three files from this repository to understand what requirements R6.1, R6.2, R7.1, R7.2 are in the ts SRD, and what code already exists. Please read these files and return their full contents:\n\n1. docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml — I need the full requirement definitions, especially R6.1, R6.2, R7.1, R7.2\n2. cmd/ts/main.go — the existing implementation\n3. cmd/ts/ts_test.go — the existing tests\n\nReturn the complete contents of all three files.","agentId":"a341d480eb8404931","agentType":"Explore","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! I have successfully read all three files. Here's the complete content:\n\n## 1. **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd004-ts.yaml** (Requirements Specification)\n\nThis file defines the complete requirements for the `ts` (timestamp) utility. Here are the specific requirements you asked about:\n\n**R6.1 & R6.2 (Relative-time parsing and age output):**\n- **R6.1**: `-r` must scan each input line for known timestamp patterns and replace each match with a human-readable relative age string (e.g., \"15m5s ago\").\n- **R6.2**: Must recognize the following timestamp patterns from the Perl source regex:\n  - Syslog format: \"Jan  5 14:30:00\"\n  - ISO-8601: \"2024-01-05T14:30:00.000Z\"\n  - RFC 2822 with optional day: \"16 Jun 94 07:29:35 GMT\"\n  - Lastlog format: \"Mon Jan  5 14:30\"\n\n**R7.1 & R7.2 (Exit codes and error handling):**\n- **R7.1**: Must exit 0 on clean EOF from stdin.\n- **R7.2**: Must exit non-zero and print a usage message to stderr when an unrecognized flag is given.\n\n## 2. **cmd/ts/main.go** (Existing Implementation)\n\nThe current implementation includes:\n- Default timestamp formatting with the format `\"%b %d %H:%M:%S\"`\n- Support for `-i` (incremental mode), `-s` (since-start mode), and `-m` (monotonic clock mode)\n- Custom format string support with strftime conversion\n- Subsecond extensions handling (%.S, %.s, %.T)\n- Proper padding and text/composite spec handling\n- SIGPIPE handler installation\n- Support for the TZ environment variable\n\n**Currently NOT implemented:** \n- The `-r` (relative-time parsing) feature (R6.1, R6.2)\n- Requirements R10 (relative-time format override)\n\n## 3. **cmd/ts/ts_test.go** (Existing Tests)\n\nThe test file includes:\n- Differential tests against the reference `ts` binary (using `testutils.BuildBinary`)\n- Tests for default multiline, single line, partial last line, and empty stdin\n- Tests for custom format strings with subsecond extensions\n- Tests for incremental and since-start modes\n- Tests for monotonic clock mode combinations\n- A `TestMutualExclusive` test that verifies `-i` and `-s` cannot both be given\n- A `TestSIGPIPE` test that validates SIGPIPE handling\n- Custom normalizers for subsecond precision and elapsed time\n\nThe tests use `testutils.TimestampNormalizer` to handle dynamic timestamps in differential testing."}],"totalDurationMs":21462,"totalTokens":29235,"totalToolUseCount":9,"usage":{"input_tokens":7,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5788,"cache_read_input_tokens":22761,"output_tokens":679,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5788},"inference_geo":""